---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About">
  <section class="hero">
    <img
      class="hero-photo"
      src="/assets/img/aboutimg.jpg"
      alt="Saramsha Dotel"
      width="104"
      height="104"
    />
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1 class="hero-greeting">Hi, I'm Saramsha.</h1>
      <p class="hero-role">Some background, in case you want it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2>Now</h2>
  <p>
    I joined <a href="https://www.wbd.com">Warner Bros. Discovery</a> in September 2025 as a senior engineer on
    the applied-AI team. The current focus is natural-language search and
    retrieval over WBD's roughly one million hours of film and television
    content, the evaluation framework our teams use to systematically compare
    embedding models, re-rankers, LLMs and prompting strategies, and the
    observability tooling that ties it all together. I also help maintain the
    internal harness we use for agent-assisted coding.
  </p>

  <h2>Naamche + reAlpha (2020–2025)</h2>
  <p>
    In September 2020 I co-founded <a href="https://www.naamche.com">Naamche</a>
    with a group of friends from college. We started as three engineers in
    Kathmandu. By the time we were acquired five years later we were forty
    people in offices in Nepal and the US, and had crossed roughly $500k in
    ARR shipping software for clients in real estate, fintech, and agri-tech.
    I was the CTO from start to finish.
  </p>
  <p>
    The work was more varied than I expected when we started. We built a
    property-management platform (myAlphie) that was later sold to Crawford
    Hoying for $6M; a property-scoring engine running predictive models on
    spatio-temporal and socio-economic data; an information retrieval tool
    for an agri-tech startup using hybrid LLM-embedding plus SPLADE search and
    re-ranking; a conversational-AI SaaS we redesigned around LLMs with
    multi-agent orchestration; and a Django fintech platform whose API latency
    we ended up cutting by about 70%.
  </p>
  <p>
    In December 2023 we were
    <a href="https://finance.yahoo.com/news/realpha-tech-corp-acquire-naamche-120000261.html">acquired</a>
    by <a href="https://www.realpha.com">reAlpha Tech Corp.</a>, a
    Nasdaq-listed proptech company — the first time a Nepali software company
    had been acquired by a Nasdaq-listed one. I stayed at reAlpha through
    September
    2025 as a senior engineer and tech lead, leading the technical development
    of their home-buying platform — natural-language search across five
    million-plus properties, AI agents that extract and validate loan
    documents, automated tour scheduling and lead follow-up. Then I moved to
    WBD.
  </p>

  <h2>Fusemachines (2019–2020)</h2>
  <p>
    My first job out of college, working on machine learning. I built
    <em>FuseExtract</em>, an OCR system for Nepali and English documents that
    was later trialed by a major Nepali bank and a telecom. I also did
    forecasting work — predicting sales and revenue for video games at
    Take-Two Interactive. Before that, briefly, I helped design the AI
    syllabus and coursework for FuseAI, an internal online course.
  </p>

  <h2>Education</h2>
  <p>
    Bachelor's in Computer Engineering from
    <a href="https://pcampus.edu.np/">Pulchowk Campus</a>, Tribhuvan
    University, 2015–2019. I graduated as batch topper with an aggregate of
    85.3% and was a three-time recipient of the Ncell Academic Excellence
    Award, given to the top student in Computer Engineering each year.
  </p>
  <p>
    During college I also finished a MicroMasters in Artificial Intelligence
    from Columbia University on edX.
  </p>

  <h2>Selected projects</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/assets/pdf/IVSP%20Paper.pdf"><strong>Disaster Assessment from Satellite Imagery</strong></a>
      — undergraduate thesis, published at IVSP 2020. Semantic segmentation
      and image classification to identify flood-affected regions in satellite
      imagery.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/writing/traffic-map/"><strong>Traffic Mobility Analytics Platform</strong></a>
      — undergraduate minor project. Computer-vision system for Kathmandu's
      roads, including a Nepali-vehicles dataset we collected to train it.
      Won the
      <a href="/achievements/smart-urban/">Smart Urban Technology Challenge</a>
      in 2018.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/achievements/hult-prize/"><strong>Hult Prize at Tribhuvan University</strong></a>
      — won locally with a team in 2017; represented Nepal at the regional
      finals in Dubai.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Else</h2>
  <p>
    I grew up in Nepal and live in New York. I read a lot — fiction mostly,
    plus history and the occasional pop-science book. I watch too much
    football, mostly Liverpool. I also like films and still play the
    occasional video game, though less than I used to.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top:2rem">
    <a href="/assets/pdf/Saramsha%20Dotel%20Resume.pdf">Resume (PDF)</a>
  </p>
</Base>
